 PINK.com, AdoreMe.com, and DailyLook.com; and other digital channels. The company also operates stores under the franchise, license, and wholesale arrangements. Victoria's Secret & Co. was incorporated in 2021 and is based in Reynoldsburg, Ohio.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Hillary  Super | CEO & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $6.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 30K people. Revenue per employee of $218K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $10K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 29\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Victorias Secret & Co. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $7.5B market cap on $6.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory. Operating margins are contracting by -2.2pp, the first warning that competitive pressure is eroding the franchise.","Returns on capital run at 18% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 8-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 36%.","The business throws off $312M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.10\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.9\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 3.9\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 10% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (16.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins softening -2.2pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.147643244519482},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (93% sell ratio, net $213.5M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 18% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Consumer Cyclical sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 8% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Victoria's Secret (VSXY) Earnings Expected to Grow: What to Know Ahead of Next Week's Release","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3035892/victoria-s-secret-vsxy-earnings-expected-to-grow-what-to-know-ahead-of-next-week-s-release?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_9-3035892","date":"2026-11-26","timesta